    "help": {
      "format": "markdown",
      "content": "\nAssign taxonomic lineages from **existing phylogenetic placements**, retaining their likelihood weights.\n\n### Inputs\n\n- A jplace JSON dataset from EPA-ng or pplacer. Its reference tree defines the placement edges.\n- A headerless, two-column tabular dataset mapping reference-tree leaf identifiers to semicolon-separated taxonomic lineages. Leaf identifiers must match the jplace reference tree.\n\nFor example, `reference_1` may map to `Bacteria;Cyanobacteria;Synechococcus`.\n\n### Outputs and interpretation\n\nThe taxonomy profile summarizes placement mass for each lineage. `LWR` and `fract` describe direct weight and its fraction; `aLWR` and `afract` include descendant taxa. `taxopath` is the semicolon-separated lineage. The labelled reference tree records the assigned lineages on the reference topology.\n\nSelect at least one output. The default selection is the taxonomy profile and labelled reference tree.\n\nSelect **per-query assignments** to inspect the same quantities for individual query names. Select **SATIVA assignments** for one lineage and a semicolon-separated list of confidences per query. Select **Krona profile** for a weight followed by separate lineage columns; its width depends on the taxonomy depth.\n\nA high placement weight supports a position relative to this reference. It does not establish that the reference taxonomy is correct or complete. Compare competing assignments before interpreting ambiguous sequences. This tool does not align sequences or perform placement searches.\n    "
    }
